WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.213
Compost at home: the two-bucket method. In the next two minutes, let us turn

2
00:00:06.213 --> 00:00:08.447
everyday kitchen waste into rich compost.

3
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:16.644
Every day our kitchens throw out vegetable peels, fruit skins and used tea

4
00:00:16.644 --> 00:00:22.422
leaves. This is wet waste. When it is dumped in a landfill, it rots, smells and

5
00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:27.478
gives off methane, a greenhouse gas. At home, the same waste can become compost,

6
00:00:27.478 --> 00:00:29.644
which is food for the soil.

7
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.574
You need two buckets with lids, some dry leaves or shredded newspaper, a little

8
00:00:36.574 --> 00:00:41.958
garden soil or old compost, and a tray or two bricks to keep the bucket off the

9
00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:42.274
floor.

10
00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:49.471
Step one. Make ten to twelve small holes on the sides and the bottom of the

11
00:00:49.471 --> 00:00:54.467
bucket, so that air can flow in. Then keep the bucket on a tray or on two

12
00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:54.761
bricks.

13
00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:02.493
Step two. Spread a five centimetre layer of dry leaves at the bottom, and add a

14
00:01:02.493 --> 00:01:07.399
handful of soil. This soil brings in the tiny microbes that do the real work.

15
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.664
Step three. Add your kitchen waste every day: peels, fruit scraps, used tea

16
00:01:14.664 --> 00:01:19.795
leaves and crushed egg shells. Cut large pieces into small bits, so that they

17
00:01:19.795 --> 00:01:20.895
break down faster.

18
00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:28.917
Step four. Every time you add wet waste, cover it with an equal handful of dry

19
00:01:28.917 --> 00:01:33.752
leaves or shredded paper, and close the lid. This keeps flies and bad smell

20
00:01:33.752 --> 00:01:34.098
away.

21
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:42.015
Do not add meat, fish or bones, milk products, or large amounts of oily or

22
00:01:42.015 --> 00:01:46.708
cooked food. And never put plastic, glass or metal in the compost bucket.

23
00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:54.461
Step five. Once a week, mix the contents with a stick. The mix should feel like

24
00:01:54.461 --> 00:01:59.713
a squeezed sponge: moist, but not dripping. If it smells bad, it is too wet, so

25
00:01:59.713 --> 00:02:02.010
add more dry leaves and mix again.

26
00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:09.337
Step six. When the first bucket is full, close it and start using the second

27
00:02:09.337 --> 00:02:14.486
one. Let the first bucket rest for about four to six weeks. The compost is ready

28
00:02:14.486 --> 00:02:19.635
when it is dark brown, crumbly and smells like fresh earth. Sieve it and use it

29
00:02:19.635 --> 00:02:21.566
in your pots and kitchen garden.

30
00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:29.213
Segregate at source. Compost at home. Wet waste is a resource, not rubbish.
